Skip a song straight away when Spotify refuses its key.

Without this, librespot carries on without the key: it downloads the song, fails to read it (the file
is encrypted), deletes the good cached copy and downloads it again, asking for the key 3 more times.
That was 5-10 seconds of silence per refused song. Only Spotify's refusal ("error audio key 0 2") is
skipped this way; a key that's just slow to arrive keeps librespot's normal behaviour. librespot.sh
applies this file. (Cadenza used to ask up to 3 times first; that only kept Spotify refusing for longer.)

diff --git a/playback/src/player.rs b/playback/src/player.rs
index f3d803d..7874308 100644
--- a/playback/src/player.rs
+++ b/playback/src/player.rs
@@ -1110,6 +1110,13 @@ impl PlayerTrackLoader {
             // parsing and bail out, so we should be safe from outputting ear-piercing noise.
             let key = match self.session.audio_key().request(track_id, file_id).await {
                 Ok(key) => Some(key),
+                // Spotify refused the key ("error audio key 0 2"). The file is encrypted,
+                // so reading it without a key only wastes a download and throws away a good cached copy
+                // before failing anyway. Give up on this track straight away. (Cadenza patch.)
+                Err(e) if e.to_string().contains("audio key error") => {
+                    warn!("Unable to load key, skipping this track: {e}");
+                    return None;
+                }
                 Err(e) => {
                     warn!("Unable to load key, continuing without decryption: {e}");
                     None
